<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2064" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄθρυπτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρύπτω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unbroken, imperishable</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1055b
			</span></i>; <i>tough</i>, of flesh, <i><span class="en">
				Herophil.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				4.596
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>not enervated, Carm. Aur.</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				35
			</span></i>; of language, <i>not affected</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέξις ἀφελὴς καὶ ἄ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Lyc.</u>
				21
			</span></i>:—of a person, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. εἰς
				γέλωτα</span>
			<i>never breaking</i> into laughter, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Per.</u>
				5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦτα ἄθρυπτα κολακείᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.38b
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fab.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			.</div>
